From 32327474eab5e88ed6121d4717f0c40549d13276 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:07:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-20: lock a component in the designer -- the lock
 of the WPF document outline (0.20.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A locked component -- and everything inside it -- cannot be dragged, resized
(no handles are shown), nudged with the arrows or moved by an alignment on
the design surface, nor deleted, cut or reordered; its position / size fields
in the property grid are disabled with a note. It can still be selected, and
its text and look can still be changed.
- The component tree: a lock on every row (open = lock it, closed = unlock),
  "🔒" in the description; the title bar has "unlock all" while something is
  locked; the design surface's right-click menu has the toggle.
- The probe is told the whole set (and gets it again with every init); a press
  on a locked component says so once, only when it would have moved; the
  selection label shows 🔒.
- The extension refuses delete / cut / order when the name or a component
  around it is locked (walks up the component tree).
- Kept per page in the workspace state like the eye; never in the source.
  The tree's contextValue is now 'component' + '.hidden' / '.locked', and the
  inline eye / lock pick their action from it.

Tests: lib 114, probe (a locked panel's button: no drag, no arrows, no handles,
refused once each), smoke 78 (tree mark, kept per page, inside-a-locked-panel
counts, delete / cut / order refused, unlock all), panels, real VS Code 80
(the real probe knows the lock, a confirmed delete inside it is refused, the
page untouched, unlock all) -- all pass; opened files MD5-unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
